license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  A harmonised panel of homicide counts and rates below the national level: about 29,000 observations for roughly 2,850 provinces, states, counties, districts, cities and police units in 78 countries, 1993 to 2025. Re-runnable pipelines extract the figures from police, statistical-office and health-ministry publications into a common schema, attach population denominators, validate against national totals and independent series, and grade each row by reliability. Every series carries its counting unit, definition flags and time basis, and a companion document compares each source's definition of homicide with the UNODC standard. Built for the Development Data Lab.
keywords:
  - homicide
  - subnational
  - crime statistics
  - official statistics
  - open data
  - UNODC
  - ICCS
